※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4615 LANG_ARENA_VALUE_GIVEN_BACK

※ A name a loop body assigns may hold, after the loop and at the top of every turn, what any
※ turn gave it: a turn is behind the next in the text and ahead of it in time.  So it is taken to
※ be made in anything the body names, as well as in what it held before the loop.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let s1: mut arena = ⎕arena
    let s2: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(s2)
    let x: mut str = "-"
    let n: mut u8 = 0u8
    while n < 2u8:
        if n = 0u8:
            x ← "a" ⧺ "b" in s1
        else:
            x ← x ⧺ "c" in s2
        n ← n + 1u8
    ⎕empty(s1)
    if x = "abc": 0u6 else: 1u6
